<header class="ref-head yr-head"><p class="cty-kicker">Year by year · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p><h1 class="research-title">1922</h1><p class="ref-lede">1922 in world history: 48 events, 16 births, 14 deaths, 3 works, 9 states founded and 10 that came to an end. 744 recorded states existed that year.</p></header>
<nav class="ref-letters yr-near" aria-label="Nearby years"><a href="/years/1918">1918</a><a href="/years/1919">1919</a><a href="/years/1920">1920</a><a href="/years/1921">1921</a><a href="/years/1922" aria-current="page">1922</a><a href="/years/1923">1923</a><a href="/years/1924">1924</a><a href="/years/1925">1925</a><a href="/years/1926">1926</a></nav>
<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Events</h2><ol class="day-events yr-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/january-11">11 January</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Insulin is first given to a diabetic patient</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Fourteen-year-old Leonard Thompson received an insulin extract at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toronto">Toronto</a> General Hospital. The first dose failed, but a purer extract made by James Collip saved his life later that month.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/october-18">18 October</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">The British Broadcasting Company is founded</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Wireless manufacturers formed the British Broadcasting Company to run <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>'s first national radio service. Under John Reith it became the public <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bbc">British Broadcasting Corporation</a> in 1927.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/november-4">4 November</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Howard Carter finds the steps to Tutankhamun's tomb</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Howard Carter's workers uncovered a step cut into the rock of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valley-of-the-kings">Valley of the Kings</a>, leading to the nearly intact <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tomb-of-tutankhamun">tomb of Tutankhamun</a>. Its treasures caused a worldwide sensation.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/november-24">24 November</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Carter uncovers the sealed doorway of Tutankhamun's tomb</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">With Lord Carnarvon present, Howard Carter's team cleared the stairway and found a sealed doorway bearing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tutankhamun">Tutankhamun</a>'s name. Two days later they looked inside.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/november-26">26 November</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Howard Carter looks into Tutankhamun's tomb</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Howard Carter made a small hole in the sealed doorway and peered in by candlelight. Asked if he could see anything, he reportedly replied, 'Yes, wonderful things.'</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/december-30">30 December</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">The Soviet Union is formally established</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Delegates from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ukraine">Ukraine</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belarus">Belarus</a> and the Transcaucasian Federation approved the treaty creating the Union of Soviet Socialist Republics. It lasted until 1991.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ukraine">Ukraine</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/march-on-rome" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/march-on-rome.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Event</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/march-on-rome">March on Rome</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The March on Rome was the mass mobilisation by which Benito Mussolini's National Fascist Party came to power in Italy in October 1922.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/abolition-of-the-ottoman-sultanate" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/abolition-of-the-ottoman-sultanate.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Event</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/abolition-of-the-ottoman-sultanate">Abolition of the Ottoman sultanate</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The abolition of the Ottoman sultanate was the decision of the Grand National Assembly in Ankara in 1922 to end the office of sultan.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-on-the-creation-of-the-ussr" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/treaty-on-the-creation-of-the-ussr.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Treaty</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/treaty-on-the-creation-of-the-ussr">Treaty on the Creation of the USSR</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Treaty on the Creation of the USSR, approved on 30 December 1922 by the First All-Union Congress of Soviets, united the Russian SFSR, the Ukrainian SSR, the Byelorussian SSR and the Transcaucasian SFSR into the Union of Soviet Socialist Republics.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/uqair-protocol" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/uqair-protocol.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Treaty</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/uqair-protocol">Uqair Protocol</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Uqair Protocol of 1922 set the borders between the Sultanate of Nejd under Ibn Saud and the British-protected Kuwait and mandated Iraq.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-dumlupinar" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-dumlupinar.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Battle</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-dumlupinar">Battle of Dumlupınar</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Battle of Dumlupınar was the decisive battle of the Greco-Turkish War, fought from 26 to 30 August 1922 in western Anatolia.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/rand-revolt" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rand-revolt.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Revolt</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/rand-revolt">Rand Revolt</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Rand Revolt was an armed uprising of white mineworkers on the Witwatersrand in 1922, sparked by mine owners' plans to cut costs by employing more black workers in semi-skilled jobs.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/washington-naval-treaty" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/washington-naval-treaty.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Treaty</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/washington-naval-treaty">Washington Naval Treaty</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Washington Naval Treaty was an arms-limitation agreement signed in February 1922 by the United States, the United Kingdom, Japan, France and Italy at the Washington Naval Conference.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Event</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/chauri-chaura-incident">Chauri Chaura incident</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Chauri Chaura incident took place on 4 February 1922 at Chauri Chaura in the Gorakhpur district of the United Provinces of British India.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Event</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/hughes-peynado-plan">Hughes–Peynado plan</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Hughes–Peynado plan was the 1922 agreement between the American secretary of state Charles Evans Hughes and the Dominican lawyer Francisco Peynado that set the terms for ending the United States occupation of the Dominican Republic.</p></div></li></ol></section>
